Subject: [PATCH] Diagnose and recover a pending test-process exit status

Temporary private validation patch for the PHP 8.3.35 OOM candidate.
Embargoed: Keep this patch private until disclosure.

The test runner checks process status without waiting after pipe EOF.
Wait using proc_close() before formatting termination status, and use
its exit code if the initial status still reports a running process.
For the hard-limit compilation test, log the initial process status and
final proc_close() result to runner stderr, outside the PHPT output.

The test and its required Termsig=9 expectation are unchanged. The next
ARM64 run must establish whether this is actually an exit-reporting race.
No production PHP runtime code is changed by this patch.

diff --git a/run-tests.php b/run-tests.php
--- a/run-tests.php
+++ b/run-tests.php
@@ -1259,6 +1259,19 @@
     }
 
     $stat = proc_get_status($proc);
+    $finalExitcode = proc_close($proc);
+
+    if (str_contains($commandline, 'oom_hard_limit_exceeded_during_complilation.php')) {
+        fwrite(STDERR, "[php-exit-diag] " . json_encode([
+            'initial_status' => $stat,
+            'proc_close_exitcode' => $finalExitcode,
+        ]) . "\n");
+    }
+
+    // Pipe EOF may precede availability of the child's exit status.
+    if ($stat['running'] && $finalExitcode >= 0) {
+        $stat['exitcode'] = $finalExitcode;
+    }
 
     if ($stat['signaled']) {
         $data .= "\nTermsig=" . $stat['stopsig'] . "\n";
@@ -1270,7 +1283,6 @@
         $data .= "\nTermsig=" . $stat["exitcode"] . "\n";
     }
 
-    proc_close($proc);
     return $data;
 }
 
